## Exercise: Configure Data Residency Controls

Set up data residency restrictions for a multi-region cloud deployment.

**AWS Data Residency Configuration:**
```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Sid": "RestrictEUDataResidency",
      "Effect": "Deny",
      "Action": [
        "s3:CreateBucket",
        "s3:PutObject",
        "rds:CreateDBInstance",
        "ec2:RunInstances"
      ],
      "Resource": "*",
      "Condition": {
        "StringNotEquals": {
          "aws:RequestedRegion": [
            "eu-west-1",
            "eu-west-2",
            "eu-central-1",
            "eu-north-1"
          ]
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

**Challenge:** Create a policy that allows data in EU regions for EU customers, but US regions for US customers, based on resource tags.

